    // exception: the first failure block in exception shape ('   <FullName> : msg', generic [[…]] allowed, known assertion
    // libraries excluded), message lines of any indentation, then its stack: the first project frame of the LAST
    // '----- Inner Stack Trace' section that has one (the innermost exception: .Result/.Wait(), reflection, wrapping),
    // else the first project frame of the outer stack. A project frame has an absolute path that is not /_/.
    // A block with none is row 11's unclassified, so tests_failed never reaches the place rule without a location.
    // A frame path is a project candidate when POSIX-absolute (not /_/) or a Windows drive path (X:\…).
    // LIMITATION: the location belongs to the FIRST exception-shaped block in the run, which need not be the planned
    // test's (the table does not know the planned test's name). Another test's exception before it, or beside the
    // planned test's assertion red, routes the run by that other location (Test is broken, or an assertion read as
    // an exception). Run the planned test filtered (--filter FullyQualifiedName=<test>) so its block is the only one.
    // compile: csc's line for a missing name (CS0117/CS1061/CS0103/CS0246/CS0234), the first one: the test file and the name;
    // for CS0117/CS1061 also (?P<type>…), the type csc says lacks the member ('Calc', 'string', 'CalcLib.Calc'), so the
