    // skips the whole class; @Disabled): run == skipped, enumerated 1..999 (no backreferences); 20: both counts >= 1000 with no
    // failure: a card, never passed. 21: a module where at least one test ran and none failed = passed, BEFORE 22-23, so a reactor
    // with test-less modules ('No tests to run.') or a test class with no @Test ('Tests run: 0') beside a green module reads passed;
    // 22-23 then fire only when NO module ran a test (one module: a test class with no @Test; no test classes; -DskipTests /
    // maven.test.skip). A reactor where one module's tests are all skipped and another is green reads no_tests_collected (a
    // refusal, not a seal). One skipped planned test among others that ran ('Tests run: 3, ..., Skipped: 1') matches 21: the
    // aggregate cannot see which; the PRODUCT REQUIREMENT in the header (the planned testcase un-skipped in TEST-*.xml) closes it.
